 second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-8x + 5y = 1; (-2x - 7y = 25) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= 1 \\\\\n8x + 28y &= -100 \\\\\n(5y + 28y) &= (1 - 100) \\\\\n33y &= -99 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -3$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 7y &= 25 \\\\\n-2x - 7(-3) &= 25 \\\\\n-2x + 21 &= 25 \\\\\n-2x &= 4 \\\\\nx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2, \\,y=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-2,-3)$." 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509051 1080 "(- \\frac{1077}{16}, \\frac{123}{8})" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509051 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509051 1083 #uuid "04912936-0284-538a-a031-970ac8ce1261" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509052 1080 "-1" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509052 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509052 1083 #uuid "079d8e57-e723-5341-8dde-001d8b14de99" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509053 1080 "4" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509053 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509053 1083 #uuid "0e23b228-36a0-5619-a7b7-a3921c993c40" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509054 1080 "-2" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509054 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509054 1083 #uuid "0e284178-f4bc-505f-90f2-2ff6238fd5eb" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17592186509055 1080 "-4" 13194139535469 17592186045443 true] [17